<section class="page-intro container"><a class="back-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}practice/`}>← Practice</a><span class="eyebrow">Practice / Teaching</span><h1>Learning through<br /><em>body and mind.</em></h1><p class="lede">University teaching in psychology and dance movement therapy.</p></section>
<section class="container detail-body"><div class="prose"><p>Alongside clinical and embodied work, I teach psychology-related courses in a university dance education setting. My teaching explores how psychological ideas can be understood not only through concepts, but also through bodily awareness, movement and experience.</p><p>Teaching interests include introductory psychology, embodied approaches, dance movement therapy, body awareness, group process and the relationship between movement, emotion and expression.</p><p>I aim to create learning spaces that connect theory with practice: inviting students to observe, reflect, experiment and develop their own thoughtful relationship with the material.</p></div><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Teaching interests</span><p>Psychology · Dance Movement Therapy · Embodied learning · Group process</p><a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/`}>Discuss teaching or collaboration <span>↗</span></a></aside></section>
